  "epistemic_guardrails": [
    "HBM shortage is not synonymous with DRAM-wafer shortage. Front-end silicon intensity, HBM stack/package production, accelerator advanced packaging, customer qualification, customer supply and platform availability are separate stages.",
    "This packet supplements already-grounded HBM3E sampling/production/customer-supply and H200 market-availability trajectories; it does not duplicate or re-promote those assets.",
    "Micron's December 2023 qualification statement proves qualification was still a distinct live stage for its HBM3E/NVIDIA program; it does not prove qualification was the universal industry bottleneck.",
    "SK hynix's Package & Test statement establishes a separate HBM back-end process after wafer fabrication and the importance of TSV/MR-MUF; it does not prove that SK hynix packaging capacity was constrained on April 11, 2024.",
    "TSMC's April 2024 statement is CoWoS/advanced-packaging capacity evidence at TSMC scope. It does not prove HBM-stack supply was abundant or that CoWoS was the only accelerator bottleneck.",
    "Micron's June 2024 approximately-3x HBM3E-versus-D5 wafer trade ratio supports silicon-intensity and non-HBM displacement mechanisms; it does not identify the immediate binding stage for HBM deliveries.",
    "No fragment may create a universal bottleneck ranking, a cross-supplier causal coefficient, or a synthetic HBM-scarcity scalar.",
    "Grounding creates EvidenceFragments only. Any cross-stage bottleneck assessment remains research-only unless separately supported by typed claims."
  ],
